{"title":"Career roadmap · Information Officer","role":"Information Officer","summary":"An Information Officer manages, organises, retrieves, evaluates, and disseminates information for libraries, research institutions, universities, government organisations, corporations, NGOs, and knowledge-intensive businesses.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career alignment"},{"type":"p","text":"An Information Officer manages, organises, retrieves, evaluates, and disseminates information for libraries, research institutions, universities, government organisations, corporations, NGOs, and knowledge-intensive businesses."},{"type":"p","text":"A BA with Library & Information Science provides a foundation in information organisation, cataloguing, classification, reference services, information retrieval, digital libraries, archives, databases, research support, and knowledge management. For stronger professional progression, students should add digital-library technologies, data skills, research methods, and information-management systems."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Typical Roles","Main Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"Entry"},{"text":"Library Intern, Information Assistant, Library Assistant"},{"text":"Information retrieval, cataloguing, user support"}],[{"text":"Early Career"},{"text":"Information Officer, Information Executive, Documentation Officer"},{"text":"Information services and documentation"}],[{"text":"Mid Career"},{"text":"Senior Information Officer, Information Specialist, Knowledge Management Executive"},{"text":"Research and knowledge systems"}],[{"text":"Advanced"},{"text":"Knowledge Manager, Information Services Manager, Digital Library Manager"},{"text":"Organisation-wide information management"}],[{"text":"Leadership"},{"text":"Head of Information Services, Chief Knowledge Officer"},{"text":"Knowledge strategy, governance and digital transformation"}],[{"text":"Specialist"},{"text":"Research Information Specialist, Digital Information Specialist"},{"text":"Research data, repositories, metadata and discovery"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build During the Degree","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Information & Library Foundations"},{"type":"h","text":"Academic foundations"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Library and Information Science fundamentals"},{"text":"Information sources and services"},{"text":"Library organisation"},{"text":"Library users and information needs"},{"text":"Basics of documentation"},{"text":"Communication skills"},{"text":"Research fundamentals"},{"text":"Computer applications"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Practical skills"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"MS Word"},{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"PowerPoint"},{"text":"Google Workspace"},{"text":"Basic database concepts"},{"text":"Internet research"},{"text":"Advanced search techniques"},{"text":"Information evaluation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project"},{"type":"h","text":"Information Resource Mapping for a College Library"},{"type":"p","text":"Create a structured database of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Books"},{"text":"Journals"},{"text":"E-books"},{"text":"Websites"},{"text":"Research databases"},{"text":"Government information sources"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Organisation & Retrieval"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on how information is structured and discovered."},{"type":"h","text":"Core areas"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cataloguing"},{"text":"Classification"},{"text":"Metadata"},{"text":"Bibliographic description"},{"text":"Indexing"},{"text":"Abstracting"},{"text":"Reference services"},{"text":"Information retrieval"},{"text":"Digital libraries"},{"text":"Documentation services"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Technologies"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"MARC concepts"},{"text":"Dublin Core"},{"text":"XML/JSON basic